# v0.16 apps: the same bytes on every platform, whatever the checkout's
# core.autocrlf (it is true on GitHub's Windows runners). A template's
# script and brief are hashed and approved by their bytes, the contract and
# the guide are handed to agents and compared by tests line by line, and
# migrations are checksummed in the database.
#
# Only files that no earlier release shipped are listed. A Windows build of
# an earlier release may have checksummed migrations 1 to 20 with the line
# endings of its checkout; changing theirs could make bzz refuse a database
# that build wrote.
